div.p:
	hi
: strongly demonstrative;
							accompanied, perhaps, with a gesture, these men here.

debeam
, subj. of characteristic: § 535(320); B. 283,1; G. 631, 2; H. 591, I (503, i);
							H.-B. 521, 1.

); H.-B. 582, I and 3, a; 
jura cogebant

							is equivalent to a verb of necessity, and hence the imperf. indic. in
							the apodosis appears with the imperf. subj. in the protasis.

auditum sit
, a general condition;
							subj. because integral part of the result clause.

major
: anomalous for the more
							usual plus or amplius;
							§407, c (247, c); B. 217, 3; G. 311, R.4;
							H.471, 4 (417, I, N.2) ; H.-B 416, d.

vos
, i.e. Chrysogonus and his
							abettors in the accusation;
